{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"37fc0791b551af38","name":"card_unit_22nd_marines","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/NavalWarfare/units/card_unit_22nd_marines","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"22nd MARINES","text":"Becomes Veteran and you draw a card when you play a Navy card.","flavorText":"Activated in June 1942 in San Diego, the 22nd Marine Regiment was initially sent to defend islands in the Pacific, training in Samoa and Hawaii before entering combat. The regiment’s first major action came in February 1944 at Eniwetok in the Marshall Islands, where they captured key islands using new fire team tactics. Later, the 22nd Marines joined the 1st Provisional Marine Brigade for the invasion of Guam in July 1944, landing near Agat and fighting for three weeks to secure the island. After Guam, the regiment became part of the 6th Marine Division and took part in the fierce Battle of Okinawa in April 1945. Landing on the northern beaches, the 22nd Marines pushed across the island and played a key role in capturing Naha and Sugar Loaf Hill, suffering heavy casualties. After WWII ended, the regiment was sent to China to help oversee the surrender and repatriation of Japanese forces before being inactivated in March 1946.","faction":"USA","type":"infantry","rarity":"Common","cost":2,"operationCost":1,"attack":2,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_22nd_marines","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_22nd_marines_title","SourceString":"22nd MARINES","LocalizedString":"22nd MARINES"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":2,"defense":3,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_22nd_marines_text","SourceString":"Becomes Veteran and you draw a card when you play a Navy card.","LocalizedString":"Becomes Veteran and you draw a card when you play a Navy card."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_22nd_marines_history","SourceString":"Activated in June 1942 in San Diego, the 22nd Marine Regiment was initially sent to defend islands in the Pacific, training in Samoa and Hawaii before entering combat. The regiment’s first major action came in February 1944 at Eniwetok in the Marshall Islands, where they captured key islands using new fire team tactics. Later, the 22nd Marines joined the 1st Provisional Marine Brigade for the invasion of Guam in July 1944, landing near Agat and fighting for three weeks to secure the island. After Guam, the regiment became part of the 6th Marine Division and took part in the fierce Battle of Okinawa in April 1945. Landing on the northern beaches, the 22nd Marines pushed across the island and played a key role in capturing Naha and Sugar Loaf Hill, suffering heavy casualties. After WWII ended, the regiment was sent to China to help oversee the surrender and repatriation of Japanese forces before being inactivated in March 1946.","LocalizedString":"Activated in June 1942 in San Diego, the 22nd Marine Regiment was initially sent to defend islands in the Pacific, training in Samoa and Hawaii before entering combat. The regiment’s first major action came in February 1944 at Eniwetok in the Marshall Islands, where they captured key islands using new fire team tactics. Later, the 22nd Marines joined the 1st Provisional Marine Brigade for the invasion of Guam in July 1944, landing near Agat and fighting for three weeks to secure the island. After Guam, the regiment became part of the 6th Marine Division and took part in the fierce Battle of Okinawa in April 1945. Landing on the northern beaches, the 22nd Marines pushed across the island and played a key role in capturing Naha and Sugar Loaf Hill, suffering heavy casualties. After WWII ended, the regiment was sent to China to help oversee the surrender and repatriation of Japanese forces before being inactivated in March 1946."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::NavalWarfare","EffectType"